    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">convertĭbĭlis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">convers-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>changeable</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">propositiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 33, 1</span></i>
			 and 2 (al. conversibilis): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deus convertibilis et demutabilis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 344</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-vertĭbĭlĭter</span></b> , <i>adv., changeably</i> (late Lat.), <i><span class="en">Aug.
				Music. 5, 13</span></i>.</div>
